win32u: with flat menus a grayed menu item is drawn once in COLOR_GRAYTEXT, as Windows does.

Seen 11-04 (Win32 tray menu with NEUTRON_SNI_DBUSMENU=0, any classic Win32 menu): grayed (disabled) items drew as
doubled, embossed text under the Neutron palette. draw_menu_item draws a disabled item twice, a white copy one pixel
down-right and then a 0x808080 copy, in FIXED colors whatever the palette. On Neutron's dark menus (Menu 43, GrayText
106) the white copy is the brightest thing in the row (near-white pixels 229 in the item's row, brightest 251).

Neutron prefixes run flat menus (UserPreferencesMask byte 2 bit 0x02, SPI_GETFLATMENU TRUE); Wine's default does not
(user_prefs byte 2 = 0x00). With flat menus Windows draws a disabled item once in COLOR_GRAYTEXT, without the emboss of
3D menus. draw_menu_item already sets COLOR_GRAYTEXT for MF_GRAYED; with flat menus it now skips the white copy and the
fixed gray, for the item text and the shortcut text. 3D menus (Wine's default) keep the emboss unchanged.

Not covered: 3D (non-flat) menus under a dark palette still emboss in fixed white/gray; owner-drawn items draw
themselves.

Lab (team "menus", 11.10-181m = 181 + this win32u.so x86_64 + i386; lab/team/menus/menutest, a File/Edit/View bar
with an enabled and a grayed item each, desk-f at 175%; the grayed row's near-white pixels / brightest pixel):
181 229 / 251; 181m 0 / 105 (2/2, single GrayText line); NEUTRON_FLAT_MENU_GRAYED=0 on 181m 229 / 251; 181m with
flat menus off for the session (SPI_SETFLATMENU FALSE) 229 / 251 (3D emboss unchanged).

Kill switch NEUTRON_FLAT_MENU_GRAYED=0.


--- a/dlls/win32u/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
@@ -1863,6 +1863,14 @@
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON flat-menu-grayed: kill switch NEUTRON_FLAT_MENU_GRAYED=0 (see draw_menu_item). */
+static BOOL neutron_flat_menu_grayed(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_FLAT_MENU_GRAYED" ); on = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    return on;
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *           NtUserTranslateAccelerator     (win32u.@)
  */
@@ -2786,7 +2794,11 @@
             if ((item->text[i] == '\t') || (item->text[i] == '\b'))
                 break;
 
-        if (item->fState & MF_GRAYED)
+        /* NEUTRON flat-menu-grayed: with flat menus (SPI_GETFLATMENU) Windows draws a disabled item once, in
+         * COLOR_GRAYTEXT (set above), without the white-and-gray emboss of 3D menus. The emboss is drawn in fixed
+         * colors, so under a dark palette its white copy stood out as doubled text (Neutron prefixes run flat
+         * menus, 2026-11-04). 3D menus keep it. Kill switch NEUTRON_FLAT_MENU_GRAYED=0. */
+        if ((item->fState & MF_GRAYED) && !(flat_menu && neutron_flat_menu_grayed()))
         {
             if (!(item->fState & MF_HILITE) )
             {
@@ -2814,7 +2826,7 @@
                 format = DT_RIGHT | DT_VCENTER | DT_SINGLELINE;
             }
 
-            if (item->fState & MF_GRAYED)
+            if ((item->fState & MF_GRAYED) && !(flat_menu && neutron_flat_menu_grayed()))
             {
                 if (!(item->fState & MF_HILITE) )
                 {
